there's been a lot of talk recently  about bitcoin miners and their  relationship to the energy grid now one  of the things that most people don't  understand is that energy grids  sometimes they have extra energy and  other times they don't have enough  energy and so naturally that volatility  between how much energy is actually  available and how much demand there is  for the energy ends up creating problems  this is where you see things like  rolling blackouts in certain states now  the bitcoin miners they have an  advantage they actually can take on as  much energy as the grid will provide and  they also can shut off in pretty much a  moment's notice and return energy back  to the grid what this allows for is more  stabilization of an energy grid if there  is surplus energy then the bitcoin  miners take it up and they go mine  bitcoin but if all of a sudden there's  an increase in demand and there needs to  be more energy put into the grid the  bitcoin miners simply shut off and they  return that energy right back to the  grid here's a recent excerpt from an  interview on fox business where susan  lee went and talked to riot blockchain  one of the largest miners in north  america about this exact issue  term mining could strain the already  shaky grid susan how can they help  stabilize the state power grid well i  can tell you that the texas power system  is pretty tricky because it requires  really a perfect balance of supply and  demand and you saw that play out in  those 2021 winter rolling blackouts when  homes couldn't get heat so this time  around in this record-breaking heat wave  texas wants to make sure that the air  conditioners continue to cool they're  turning to a new source and that is  cryptocurrency mining and bitcoin miners  and how exactly are you helping out the  texas power grid so riot made  significant investment and made  significant commitments in the power  grid here and that has driven more  generation and helped stabilize the grid  but with that energy we secured we have  the unique property of being flexible  enough to provide that power back to the  grid when it is in high demand right so  basically you power up when there's  excess capacity and you power down when  there's a lot of usage and the state  needs more electricity for the in order  to cool the homes across this uh the  state exactly and that's very unique to  bitcoin mining not most most large  energy loads cannot just shut on and off  you know throughout the day we have the  flexibility because bitcoin blocks come  10 minutes apart and that's as much work  as we're doing yeah and also stu you  know they've uh they've purchased their  electricity and their power usage on a  10-year contractual basis already  now it's great to see this aspect of  bitcoin mining getting much more  attention plenty of people are yelling  and screaming they're critiquing bitcoin  mining they're saying it consumes too  much energy the truth is on the ground  bitcoin miners are helping to stabilize  energy grids and they provide for better  planning for many of these energy  companies ultimately bitcoin mining is  improving american infrastructure it's  not going anywhere and in fact my guess  is that many energy grids around the  country are going to start inviting  bitcoin miners there because they  understand the benefits and it solves  one of their most pressing problems hey  you did you like this video great we  make five of them a day and post them  here on this channel make sure you  subscribe like the video and see you  next time
 

